em;\"><mjx-TeXAtom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c49\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c49\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c49\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D416 TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-utext style=\"font-size: 88.4%; padding: 0.848em 0 0.226em 0;\" variant=\"bold\">𝛍</mjx-utext></mjx-mi><mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2016\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\" fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">W</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">μ</mi><msup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\" fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>III</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">W</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">μ</mi><msup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>,\nso that the Type II test is at least as powerful. <em>Hint:</em> both\nare squared distances from <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf{W}\\boldsymbol{\\upmu}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria